window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-866d18fe9ed30c97"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"moving-your-custom-gpt-workflows-to-plugins\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"gpt\">将自定义 GPT 工作流迁移到插件</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面的 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>自定义 GPT 让你可以按自己的方式使用 ChatGPT。插件在此基础上进一步扩展，把你的指令和知识带入能够完成更多工作的工作流。</p> <p>本指南适用于 ChatGPT Enterprise 工作区管理员，以及要迁移自己创建的 GPT 的用户。请从适合你角色的路径开始：</p> <ul> <li><strong>工作区管理员：</strong><a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=plan-your-transition\">准备工作区</a>、检查权限，并<a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=admin-bulk-migration\">批量迁移 GPT</a>。</li> <li><strong>GPT 创建者：</strong><a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=identify-gpts-that-may-need-extra-attention\">准备你的 GPT</a>，然后<a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=migrate-test-and-share\">迁移、测试并分享</a>。</li> </ul> <p><strong>要使用别人创建的 GPT？</strong> 请让该 GPT 的创建者或工作区管理员负责迁移，然后<a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=step-3-share-and-verify-access\">安装对方分享给你的替代品</a>。</p> <p><strong>创建或完善插件</strong></p> <p>有关如何构建新插件，或在迁移后更新插件，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-0d81218eacd2463c\">构建插件</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"understand-the-change\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">了解变化</h2> <p>我们正在将自定义 GPT 逐步转为插件。请根据以下里程碑，在自定义 GPT 停用之前规划迁移。</p> <p><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001256-plugins-in-chatgpt-and-codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件（需联网）</a>是用于工作流的可复用软件包，可包含技能、应用或两者。 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001066\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>技能</strong>（需联网）</a>说明如何完成一项任务，例如按照团队风格撰写内容。<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11487775\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>应用</strong>（需联网）</a>将 ChatGPT 连接到其他服务，以获取信息或执行受支持的操作。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图说明：插件是用于工作流的软件包。它可以包含技能（提供完成工作的指引）、应用（连接工具和信息），也可以两者兼有。</p> </blockquote> <p>在 Enterprise 工作区中，<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11509118\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">你的管理员（需联网）</a>决定你可以使用哪些插件；在支持的情况下，还可以按角色控制访问。管理员可以让你自行安装插件，也可以为符合条件的用户自动安装。分享插件或将插件发布到工作区需要单独的权限。</p> <p><strong>你现有的权限仍然有效</strong></p> <p>插件遵循你的<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001256-plugins-in-chatgpt-and-codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">现有应用访问权限（需联网）</a>。例如，通过 ChatGPT 登录 Google Drive 后，其插件可以处理你的账号本来就有权访问的文档；这不会解锁其他文件，也不会新增 Google Drive 权限。</p> <p>你可能需要<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001494\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">连接账号（需联网）</a>或<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001495\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">批准某项操作（需联网）</a>。可用功能取决于你的应用访问权限、工作区设置，以及使用 ChatGPT 的入口。</p> <p>只包含技能和参考文件的插件无需连接应用。对于每个必需的应用，用户都需要拥有相应访问权限，并完成工作流所需的账号连接或操作授权。如果某个可选应用不可用，其他功能仍可能正常工作；但依赖该应用的功能无法使用。</p> <p><strong>插件页面示例</strong></p> <p>下面是一个插件页面示例，展示了它的应用和技能。<strong>Disabled by admin（管理员已停用）</strong>标签表示此示例插件在该工作区中不可使用。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图说明：Intuit QuickBooks 插件页面示例，标出了可用状态、示例请求、描述、已连接应用和包含的技能。</p> </blockquote> <p>使用自定义 GPT 时，你需要明确<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8554407-gpts-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">选择 GPT（需联网）</a>（在 ChatGPT 网页端打开它，或通过 @ 提及它），然后再发送请求。</p> <p>使用插件时，你可以直接选择可用的插件或技能。在 ChatGPT 中，也可以<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001256-plugins-in-chatgpt-and-codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">使用 @ 提及，或打开 + 并选择 More（需联网）</a>；具体方式取决于当前入口是否支持。</p> <p><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/docs/codex/migrate-custom-gpts/invoke-plugin-hq.webm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">从 ChatGPT 输入框中选择插件（需联网）</a></p> <figcaption> 从输入框中选择一个可用插件，然后说明你希望它协助完成什么任务。 </figcaption> <p>你也可以直接描述任务：如果某个已安装技能的说明与你的需求相符，ChatGPT 可以<a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23?anchor=how-chatgpt-and-codex-use-skills\">自动使用该技能</a>，包括打包在插件中的技能。</p> <p><strong>测试插件的选择方式</strong></p> <p>自动选择技能取决于任务和可用能力；已安装的插件不会在每次请求中都运行。迁移后，请同时测试明确选择插件和直接提出普通任务请求这两种方式。</p> <p><a id=\"what-can-a-plugin-do-compared-with-a-custom-gpt\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"gpt_1\">插件与自定义 GPT 有什么不同？</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>你的目标</th> <th>使用自定义 GPT</th> <th>使用插件</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>复用指令</td> <td>你可以向 GPT 添加指令来引导回答。</td> <td>技能可以提供可复用的指引，说明如何完成任务。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>使用团队知识</td> <td>你可以上传参考文件作为 GPT 的知识。</td> <td>技能可以包含参考文件。请检查迁移后的资源，并测试它们的使用方式。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>连接其他服务</td> <td>自定义操作可以将 GPT 连接到外部服务。</td> <td>应用负责连接服务并提供受支持的操作。自定义 GPT 操作需要单独重建。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>使用工具并创建文件</td> <td>你可以启用网页搜索、图像生成和数据分析等可用能力。</td> <td>可用工具取决于使用入口和工作区设置。请测试团队需要的输出。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>启动工作流</td> <td>你可以打开或明确选择 GPT。</td> <td>你可以选择插件或技能；ChatGPT 也可能自动使用相关的已安装技能。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>与团队分享</td> <td>你可以将 GPT 分享给获准的受众。</td> <td>你可以根据工作区权限分享或发布插件。推出前请检查访问权限。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h4>哪些内容会迁移到插件</h4> <p><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/docs/codex/migrate-custom-gpts/01-what-transfers-hq.mp4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">迁移到插件的内容（需联网）</a></p> <p><figcaption id=\"01-what-transfers-description\"> <strong> 了解哪些内容会迁移到插件，哪些需要重新构建。 </strong> 查看 GPT 的指令和参考文件如何变成技能，以及已连接的应用如何继续属于插件。自定义操作不会迁移；请计划使用受支持应用的读取或写入操作，或自定义 MCP 服务器来替代它们。 </figcaption> </p> <p><a id=\"plan-your-transition\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"for-admins-prepare-your-workspace\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">管理员：准备工作区</h2> <p>帮助团队延续现有工作：确定迁移负责人、检查相应权限，并规划替代插件的访问方式。</p> <ul> <li><strong>管理员通知。</strong>管理员会提前收到通知和指引，以规划过渡并为团队做好准备。</li> <li><strong>迁移。</strong>GPT 创建者和工作区管理员可以将已发布的 GPT 迁移为插件。</li> <li><strong>自定义 GPT 停用。</strong>自定义 GPT 将停止运行。请将希望保留的工作流迁移到插件，并在停用前完成测试。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"choose-priority-migrations\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">选择优先迁移项</h3> <p>先从团队最依赖的 GPT 开始。与创建者商定要保留哪些内容、由谁维护，以及谁需要访问权限。</p> <ul> <li>为自定义操作留出额外时间，因为它们需要单独重建。</li> <li>为每个 GPT 指定负责人，并记录其用途、受众、指令、参考文件和集成。</li> <li>请负责人保存几个熟悉的提示词和理想结果，其中包括一个较难的案例，以便与替代品进行比较。</li> <li>确认哪些 GPT 已发布。趁仍可创建 GPT 时，请创建者发布需要保留的草稿；不要求公开分享。</li> </ul> <h4>选择优先工作流</h4> <p><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/docs/codex/migrate-custom-gpts/02-prioritize-workflows-hq.mp4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">选择优先工作流（需联网）</a></p> <p><figcaption id=\"02-prioritize-workflows-description\"> <strong> 根据负责人和近期使用情况确定 GPT 迁移的优先级。 </strong> 找出团队仍在依赖的 GPT，并考虑放弃不再使用的工作流。拥有 ChatGPT 管理员插件访问权限的管理员，可以请求过去 30 天内的 GPT 名称、负责人和消息数量，帮助确定优先级。 </figcaption> </p> <p><a id=\"review-workspace-permissions\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">检查工作区权限</h3> <p>迁移之前，请检查每个人是否都具备所需访问权限。权限控制使用、分享或发布插件等操作；角色则会将承担相似职责的权限组合在一起。通过<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11750701\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">基于角色的访问控制（RBAC）（需联网）</a>，工作区所有者可以为个人或群组分配角色。</p> <p>请使用下表检查迁移和替代插件所需的访问权限。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>操作</th> <th>管理员应检查的内容</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>将自己创建的自定义 GPT 迁移为插件</td> <td>为工作区启用插件。执行迁移的人必须是该 GPT 的创建者、工作区所有者或管理员，并且该 GPT 必须已发布。仅拥有他人 GPT 的访问权限并不足以迁移。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>将新迁移的 GPT（现为插件）分享给个人或群组</td> <td>为需要向个人或群组分享替代插件的人授予 <strong>Share plugins</strong> 权限。只使用插件的人不需要此权限。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>将新迁移的 GPT（现为插件）发布到工作区目录</td> <td>为需要在工作区插件目录发布替代品的人授予 <strong>Publish plugins to workspace</strong> 权限。此权限与直接分享不同。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>安装并使用新插件</td> <td>为目标用户或角色启用 <strong>Use plugins</strong>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>使用包含的应用</td> <td>为目标用户或角色启用所需应用，并确认其已连接账号可以访问所需信息。只能执行受支持且获准的操作，并且仍须获得必要批准。安装插件不会新增应用或文件权限。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><strong>内置迁移无需上传权限</strong></p> <p>仅使用内置迁移功能时，无需启用 <strong>Upload plugins</strong> 或 <strong>Upload plugins with custom MCP servers</strong>。对于单独重建的集成，请按照工作区政策设置相应权限。</p> <p>当前设置说明请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11509118\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件和应用管理员控制（需联网）</a>以及<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001066\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">技能管理员控制（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"check-installation-and-app-access\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">检查安装方式和应用访问权限</h3> <p>决定团队成员如何获取每个替代插件。<strong>Available（可用）</strong>允许符合条件的用户自行安装插件；<strong>Installed（已安装）</strong>则会为符合条件的用户或角色安装插件。这些设置不会改变插件的分享对象。</p> <p>请分别检查所需应用：核实工作区和角色访问权限、账号登录状态以及操作批准流程。使用与普通团队成员权限相同的账号测试访问。</p> <p><a id=\"admin-bulk-migration\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"for-workspace-admins-migrate-gpts-in-bulk\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"gpt_2\">工作区管理员：批量迁移 GPT</h4> <p>在 ChatGPT Work 中输入 <strong>@</strong> 并选择 <a href=\"#/article/a-f094a985d5b867ef\">ChatGPT Admin</a>。检查其中的 Admin 应用是否显示 <strong>Connected（已连接）</strong>。在 Codex 中，请使用下方提示词旁边的打开或复制按钮。发送之前，请审核提示词和所选插件。</p> <p><a id=\"1-inventory-and-prioritize\"></a> <a id=\"1-choose-the-gpts\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"1-run-the-gpt-report\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"1-gpt\">1. 生成 GPT 报告</h3> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) Run the GPT report prioritizing by most recently used GPTs in the last 30 days.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) 请运行 GPT 报告，优先列出过去 30 天内最近使用过的 GPT。</div></div> <p>报告按近期使用情况排序，并包含负责人、使用情况、迁移状态和自定义操作。</p> <p><a id=\"optional-add-report-details\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_6\">可选：添加报告详情</h4> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) Run the GPT report and include a summary of GPTs that haven’t been migrated.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) 请运行 GPT 报告，并附上尚未迁移的 GPT 的摘要。</div></div> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) Run the GPT report and include which GPTs have knowledge files attached.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) 请运行 GPT 报告，并注明哪些 GPT 附有知识文件。</div></div> <p><a id=\"2-create-one-migration-tracker\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"2-export-and-use-the-results\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"2\">2. 导出并使用结果</h3> <p>选择你偏好的格式，例如 <strong>Excel</strong>、<strong>CSV</strong> 或 <strong>Google Sheets</strong>。可以按自己的需要排序、筛选、分享或跟踪迁移进度。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) Run the GPT report and export it as [preferred format].\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) 请运行 GPT 报告，并将其导出为 [preferred format]。</div></div> <p><a id=\"6-help-teams-switch-and-repeat\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"3-schedule-a-recurring-report\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"3\">3. 安排定期报告</h3> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) Run the GPT report for [workspace] every [day] at [time and time zone]. Post the results here.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) 请在每个 [day] 的 [time and time zone]，为 [workspace] 运行 GPT 报告。将结果发布在这里。</div></div> <p>任务必须启用<a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">计划任务</a>，并且 Admin 插件必须可供该任务使用。请在 <strong>Scheduled（已安排）</strong>中检查计划和首次运行结果。</p> <p><a id=\"3-migrate-a-small-batch\"></a> <a id=\"2-migrate-a-small-batch\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"4-migrate-selected-gpts\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"4-gpt\">4. 迁移选定的 GPT</h3> <p>按 GPT ID 选择，或描述一个群组，例如所有私有 GPT。迁移生成的替代品默认是私有状态，原 GPT 将变为只读。</p> <p><strong>批量迁移不会沿用分享设置</strong></p> <p>批量迁移<strong>不会复制分享设置</strong>。请记录哪些人需要访问，然后<strong>手动分享每个替代品</strong>，或让 GPT 创建者来分享。我们预计 Admin 插件之后会支持批量分享。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) Migrate [GPT IDs or a description of the GPTs] to plugins. Show me the selection and ask for confirmation before migrating.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) 请将 [GPT IDs or a description of the GPTs] 迁移为插件。先向我展示所选对象，并在迁移之前请求确认。</div></div> <p><a id=\"4-test-and-refine\"></a> <a id=\"3-have-owners-test\"></a> <a id=\"5-share-and-check-access\"></a> <a id=\"4-share-and-confirm-access\"></a></p> <p>请负责人<a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=step-2-test-with-familiar-work\">测试替代插件</a>并验证访问权限。自定义操作需要单独重建。</p> <p><a id=\"migration-email-template\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"email-template-ask-gpt-creators-to-migrate\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"gpt-gpt\">邮件模板：请 GPT 创建者迁移 GPT</h4> <p>发送前请按实际情况修改此模板，并替换其中的占位符。</p> <p><strong>邮件模板：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Subject: Please migrate your custom GPTs by [deadline]\n\nHi [name],\n\nWe’re moving our custom GPT workflows to plugins. Please migrate, test, and share these GPTs by [deadline]:\n\n[GPT names/links]\n\nIf you no longer need one, let us know. For those you’re keeping:\n\n1. Migrate. Save the intended audience and finish important edits first. Go to My GPTs &gt; Created by me &gt; Migrate to plugin. The GPT must be published; after migration, it becomes read-only.\n\n2. Test. Try familiar tasks and one harder case. Check the instructions, attached files, results, and required apps or tools.\n\n3. Share. Each replacement starts private. Share it with the intended people or groups, then ask a teammate to test access. Keep private workflows private.\n\nFollow [migration guide link] for the steps. Custom actions need rebuilding; contact [admin contact] if yours uses them or you need help.\n\nPlease reply with each plugin’s link, testing status, and any blockers.\n\nThanks for helping your team make the switch,\n[admin name/team]\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>模板中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">主题：请在 [deadline] 前迁移你的自定义 GPT\n\n[name]，你好：\n\n我们正在将自定义 GPT 工作流程迁移到插件。请在 [deadline] 前迁移、测试并分享以下 GPT：\n\n[GPT names/links]\n\n如果某个 GPT 已经不再需要，请告诉我们。对于你要保留的 GPT：\n\n1. 迁移。先记录预期受众，并完成重要编辑。前往 My GPTs（我的 GPT）&gt; Created by me（由我创建）&gt; Migrate to plugin（迁移为插件）。GPT 必须已发布；迁移后，它将变为只读。\n\n2. 测试。尝试熟悉的任务，以及一个难度更高的场景。检查指令、附加文件、结果，以及必需的应用或工具。\n\n3. 分享。每个替代插件最初均为私有状态。将它分享给预期的人员或群组，然后请一位队友测试访问权限。私有工作流程应继续保持私有。\n\n具体步骤请参照 [migration guide link]。自定义操作需要重新构建；如果你的 GPT 使用了自定义操作，或你需要帮助，请联系 [admin contact]。\n\n请回复每个插件的链接、测试状态，以及任何阻碍。\n\n感谢你帮助团队完成切换，\n[admin name/team]</div></div> <p><a id=\"identify-gpts-that-may-need-extra-attention\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"for-gpt-creators-prepare-your-gpt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"gpt-gpt_1\">GPT 创建者：准备你的 GPT</h2> <p>迁移自己创建的 GPT 之前，请保存它的目标受众，以及一些熟悉的提示词和结果用于测试。查看下表，找出需要额外关注的部分。管理员代替创建者迁移时，应与创建者一起确认这些详情。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>如果你的自定义 GPT……</th> <th>需要检查的内容</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>使用自定义操作</td> <td>自定义操作不会迁移。请通过受支持的连接器或<a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?sectionMissing=replacing-a-gpt-custom-action\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">自定义 MCP 连接（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>重新构建所需集成，并在团队切换之前测试。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>依赖特定模型、详细指令或严格格式</td> <td>所选模型不会迁移；Enterprise 默认设置会生效。请比较熟悉的提示词和结果。确认已选择正确技能，并且它遵循指令和格式，因为行为可能有所不同。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>依赖文件、工具或先前对话上下文</td> <td>检查所需文件、模板和示例是否存在并被正确使用；迁移与检索行为可能不同。测试必需工具，例如网页搜索、图像、数据分析或文件创建。GPT 的能力设置不能保证新环境完全相同。对话开场白和先前聊天可能不会复制，因此请保存有用的提示词，并标记所需上下文。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>与队友或工作区外的人分享</td> <td>记录目标受众，并确认他们能够安装和使用替代品。向用户说明如何安装或选择它，并检查替代品的分享设置。检查外部用户的访问权限：受影响的 Enterprise 工作区会包含公开 GPT，但其他套餐的公开分享情况和时间安排可能不同。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>过渡期间仍需更新</td> <td>原 GPT 在停用之前仍可使用。随着工作流变化，应维护并测试替代插件。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"migrate-test-and-share\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"for-gpt-creators-migrate-test-and-share\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"gpt_3\">GPT 创建者：迁移、测试并分享</h2> <p>以下步骤适用于你创建的已发布 GPT。工作区管理员也可以用这些步骤帮助创建者单独迁移 GPT。</p> <p><strong>迁移之前：</strong>迁移后，原 GPT 会变成只读。停用之前你仍可继续使用，但之后的编辑必须在替代插件中进行。</p> <p><a id=\"step-1-convert-your-gpt\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"1-gpt_1\">步骤 1：转换 GPT</h3> <p>前往 <strong>My GPTs（我的 GPT）</strong>，在 <strong>Created by me（由我创建）</strong>中找到 GPT，然后选择 <strong>Migrate to plugin（迁移到插件）</strong>。也可以请工作区管理员提供帮助。</p> <p>迁移会将 GPT 指令转换为技能，并带上知识文件和已连接的应用。自定义操作需要单独重建。请保存熟悉的提示词：对话开场白不会一一迁移。所选模型不会迁移，能力设置也不能保证使用相同工具或呈现相同行为。分享之前，请检查迁移后的文件并测试所需工具。</p> <p>如果看不到 <strong>Migrate to plugin（迁移到插件）</strong>，请参阅管理员常见问题中的<a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?sectionMissing=why-dont-i-see-the-migration-option\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">为什么我看不到迁移选项？（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>。</p> <p>新插件默认是私有状态。测试之后，再将它分享给需要访问的人，即使他们原本已经可以使用旧 GPT 也一样。</p> <p><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/docs/codex/migrate-custom-gpts/03-migration-walkthrough-hq.mp4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">观看迁移工作流（需联网）</a></p> <p><figcaption id=\"03-migration-walkthrough-description\"> <strong> 按照迁移步骤操作，然后审核并安装插件。 </strong> 此视频展示的是较早版本的应用界面。当前应用中，请在左侧导航中选择 <strong>Customize（自定义）</strong>，然后选择 <strong>Plugins（插件）</strong>来查找插件。 </figcaption> </p> <p><a id=\"step-2-test-with-familiar-work\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"2_1\">步骤 2：使用熟悉的工作进行测试</h3> <p>先让插件处理熟悉的任务，再测试一个更困难的案例。分享之前，请检查以下内容：</p> <ul> <li>是否选择了正确的技能？它是否遵循你的指令？</li> <li>它是否使用了预期的参考资料，并按要求的结构、字段和格式生成完整答案或文件？</li> <li>它是否正确处理较难案例，并能在可接受的时间内作出响应？</li> <li>它所需的工具和集成是否可用？</li> </ul> <p><strong>工作流准备好之后再切换</strong></p> <p>如果缺少某项必需能力，在找到并测试替代方案之前，请不要切换该工作流。</p> <p><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/docs/codex/migrate-custom-gpts/04-test-and-share-hq.mp4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">分享前先测试（需联网）</a></p> <p><figcaption id=\"04-test-and-share-description\"> <strong> 分享插件之前，先测试熟悉的工作流并进行完善。 </strong> </figcaption> </p> <p><a id=\"step-3-share-and-verify-access\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"3_1\">步骤 3：分享并验证访问权限</h3> <p>检查哪些人能够访问新插件。要分享给个人或群组，你需要 <strong>Share plugins</strong> 权限；要发布到工作区，你需要 <strong>Publish plugins to workspace</strong> 权限。请让目标用户打开替代品并进行测试。</p> <p><strong>对于使用替代品的人：</strong>创建者或管理员分享插件之后，你需要先安装它才能使用；除非管理员已经为你安装。</p> <p>如果你无法分享或发布插件，应先请管理员检查你的权限，再宣布团队切换。</p> <p><a id=\"step-4-help-your-team-switch\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"4\">步骤 4：帮助团队切换</h3> <p>分享替代品链接，说明主要差异，并演示一个熟悉的任务。更新入职资料、指引和已保存的资源，并指定后续变更和问题的负责人。</p> <p>迁移后，插件创建者、工作区所有者或管理员可以<a href=\"#/article/a-0d81218eacd2463c\">编辑替代品</a>。每次更改后都应重新运行重要测试。</p> <p><a id=\"what-happens-to-the-original-gpt\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"gpt_4\">原 GPT 会发生什么？</h3> <p>在停用之前，原 GPT 仍可使用；即使停止创建新 GPT，你仍可以编辑尚未迁移的现有 GPT。迁移某个 GPT 后，原 GPT 会变为只读。到停用时，自定义 GPT 将停止运行并从 GPT 目录中移除。</p> <p><a id=\"troubleshoot-common-blockers\"></a> <a id=\"details-still-being-confirmed\"></a> <a id=\"additional-migration-questions\"></a> <a id=\"can-i-migrate-gpts-on-behalf-of-my-customers-or-users-including-in-bulk\"></a> <a id=\"can-we-migrate-or-recover-a-gpt-after-the-retirement-date\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"admin-faq\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">管理员常见问题</h2> <p>以下是有关准备工作区并帮助团队切换的一些常见问题。</p> <p><a id=\"preparing-your-workspace\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">准备工作区</h3> <p><a id=\"gpt\"></a> <strong>管理员可以一次迁移多个 GPT 吗？</strong></p> <p>可以。工作区管理员可以使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-f094a985d5b867ef\">ChatGPT Admin 插件</a>迁移选定的批次。请从团队最需要的 GPT 开始。</p> <p>使用<a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=admin-bulk-migration\">管理员操作指南</a>生成报告并迁移选定的 GPT。批量迁移不会沿用分享设置，因此要手动分享每个替代品。</p> <p><a id=\"gpt-1\"></a> <strong>谁可以迁移 GPT？流程是什么？</strong></p> <p>GPT 创建者或工作区管理员可以从已发布 GPT 的页面启动迁移。即使管理员不是创建者，也可以执行迁移。</p> <p>必须启用插件。仅拥有分享访问权限，并不意味着有权迁移 GPT。</p> <p><strong>为什么我看不到迁移选项？</strong></p> <p>你必须是 GPT 创建者或工作区管理员；GPT 必须已发布；并且你必须已启用插件。</p> <p>能使用别人的 GPT，并不代表你有权迁移它。</p> <p>如果满足以上条件但仍看不到该选项，请联系 OpenAI 支持，并提供 GPT 名称、所有者和你遇到的问题描述。</p> <p><a id=\"-1\"></a> <strong>在用户开始迁移之前，我应检查哪些权限？</strong></p> <p>先启用插件。内置迁移工作流不要求启用 Upload plugins 或 Upload plugins with custom MCP servers。</p> <p>要在工作区内与他人分享插件，需要 Share plugins；要在整个工作区发布插件，需要 Publish plugins to workspace。</p> <p>重建自定义集成是单独的任务，可能需要其他权限。</p> <p><a id=\"-2\"></a> <strong>员工使用迁移后的插件需要什么权限？</strong></p> <p>员工需要：</p> <ul> <li><strong>Use plugins</strong> 权限。</li> <li>替代插件的访问权限。</li> <li>允许他们安装插件或由管理员为他们安装插件的工作区政策。</li> </ul> <p>任何包含的应用仍需要相应的应用访问权限和授权。通过 ChatGPT 连接账号，并不会使用户在该应用中获得额外权限。</p> <p><a id=\"chat-work\"></a> <strong>员工可以在 Chat 中使用迁移后的插件，还是必须使用 Work？</strong></p> <p>为用户启用插件后，迁移后的插件既可在 Chat 中使用，也可在 Work 中使用。可用工具仍取决于插件、工作区设置和使用入口。有关创建和编辑工作流及其前置条件，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-0d81218eacd2463c\">构建插件</a>。</p> <p>请分别检查每项任务的访问权限：使用插件、创建或编辑插件，以及分享或发布插件。指定维护者之前，请让管理员确认他们能够进入创建和编辑界面；内置迁移所需权限并不能回答这个问题。</p> <p><a id=\"-3\"></a> <strong>推出替代品时应如何管理访问权限？</strong></p> <p>检查每个插件的目标受众和<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11509118\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">安装政策（需联网）</a>，然后请目标受众中的某个人测试访问。</p> <p><strong>Available（可用）</strong>表示符合条件的用户可以自行安装；<strong>Installed（已安装）</strong>表示默认会为这些用户安装。角色控制和应用权限仍然有效。</p> <p>替代品默认是私有状态。能够访问原 GPT，并不会自动获得插件访问权限。请将插件分享给目标个人或群组，然后让接收者安装并测试；除非管理员已经为他们安装。还应指定后续维护者，以便管理替代品并协助队友处理访问问题。</p> <p><a id=\"testing-and-ongoing-administration\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">测试和持续管理</h3> <p><a id=\"gpt-2\"></a> <strong>迁移后的插件会与原 GPT 完全一样吗？</strong></p> <p>迁移后的插件可能与原 GPT 的响应不同。使用相同的提示词和参考文件进行比较，其中应包括一个较难的示例；检查答案是否引用正确来源、包含预期事实、遵循要求的格式并使用所需工具。同时测试明确选择插件和普通任务请求两种方式，因为自动选择技能取决于请求和可用能力。请负责人评估：</p> <ul> <li>输出质量。</li> <li>遵循指令的程度。</li> <li>完成任务所需的时间。</li> </ul> <p>GPT 原本选择的模型不会迁移；会使用 Enterprise 默认设置。</p> <p><a id=\"gpt-3\"></a> <strong>使用自定义操作的 GPT 应如何处理？</strong></p> <p>自定义操作不会通过迁移工作流转移。维护该工作流的人需要使用受支持的连接器或自定义 MCP 服务器重建集成。有关步骤和可改编的提示词，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?sectionMissing=replacing-a-gpt-custom-action\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">替换 GPT 自定义操作（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>。</p> <p>应尽早识别这些 GPT，以便技术和安全团队有时间审核替代品及其权限。</p> <p><a id=\"gpt-4\"></a> <strong>迁移后原 GPT 会怎样？</strong></p> <p>原 GPT 在停用前仍可使用。停用时，自定义 GPT 将停止运行并从 GPT 目录中移除。</p> <p>之后由所有者维护插件。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=what-happens-to-the-original-gpt\">原 GPT 会发生什么？</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"gpt-5\"></a> <strong>停用后还能迁移 GPT 吗？</strong></p> <p>可以。停用之后仍然可以迁移 GPT，但该 GPT 本身将无法继续运行。</p> <p><a id=\"-4\"></a> <strong>迁移后适用哪些管理员控制？</strong></p> <p>迁移后的插件遵循工作区的<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001256-plugins-in-chatgpt-and-codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件权限（需联网）</a>。管理员可以控制哪些人能使用和分享插件，以及哪些人能将插件发布到工作区。你可以查看角色权限并管理单个插件。</p> <p>包含的应用仍保留各自的访问和操作控制，因此让插件可用并不会授予用户访问其应用数据或操作的权限。</p> <p><a id=\"-5\"></a> <strong>管理员应如何规划插件用量和费用？</strong></p> <p>将自定义 GPT 转换为插件不会消耗额度。若采用基于额度的计费，编辑或更新插件会消耗额度。转换与使用替代插件是分开的，因此推出之前应分别检查工作流的用量和费用。</p> <p>用量取决于插件在 Chat 还是 Work 中运行、涉及哪些模型和功能，以及工作区协议。基于额度的计费下，Instant Chat 通常不限量，但请求可能切换到推理模型，或使用会消耗额度的功能。Work 的额度消耗取决于所用模型和 Token 数量。以美元计费的 Enterprise 协议条款不同，其中可能包括 Instant 用量费用。推出之前，请查看工作区的<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11481834\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">额度计费费率表（需联网）</a>或<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001415\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">美元计费费率表（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>请分别检查用户实际生效的使用限额和工作区支出控制。在基于额度的工作区中，将超额用量限额设为零可以阻止超出共享额度分配的消费，但不会阻止使用剩余额度。用量提醒会通知管理员，但不会停止用量。请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001001\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">管理使用限额和超额用量（需联网）</a>，了解适用于你工作区的控制措施。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"moving-your-custom-gpt-workflows-to-plugins\">Moving your custom GPT workflows to plugins</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Custom GPTs helped you make ChatGPT your own. Plugins build on that work, bringing your instructions and knowledge into workflows that can do more.</p> <p>This guide is for ChatGPT Enterprise workspace admins and people migrating GPTs they created. Start with the path that fits your role:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Workspace admins:</strong> <a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=plan-your-transition\">Prepare your workspace</a>, check permissions, and <a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=admin-bulk-migration\">migrate GPTs in bulk</a>.</li> <li><strong>GPT creators:</strong> <a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=identify-gpts-that-may-need-extra-attention\">Prepare your GPT</a>, then <a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=migrate-test-and-share\">migrate, test, and share it</a>.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Using someone else’s GPT?</strong> Ask its creator or a workspace admin to migrate it, then <a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=step-3-share-and-verify-access\">install the replacement they share with you</a>.</p> <p><strong>Create or refine a plugin</strong></p> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-0d81218eacd2463c\">Build plugins</a> for guidance on building a new plugin or updating one after migration.</p> <h2 id=\"understand-the-change\">Understand the change</h2> <p>We’re transitioning custom GPTs to plugins. Use the milestones below to plan your migration before custom GPTs are retired.</p> <p>A <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001256-plugins-in-chatgpt-and-codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">plugin (online)</a> is a reusable package for a workflow that can include skills, apps, or both. <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001066\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>Skills</strong> (online)</a> explain how to do a task, such as writing in your team's style. <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11487775\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>Apps</strong> (online)</a> connect ChatGPT to other services for information or supported actions.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: A plugin is a package for a workflow. It can include skills, which provide instructions for how to do the work, apps, which connect to tools and information, or both.</p> </blockquote> <p>In an enterprise workspace, <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11509118\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">your admin (online)</a> decides which plugins you can use, including access by role where supported. They can make plugins available for you to install or install them automatically for eligible users. Sharing a plugin or publishing it to the workspace requires separate permissions.</p> <p><strong>Your existing permissions still apply</strong></p> <p>Plugins respect your <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001256-plugins-in-chatgpt-and-codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">existing app access (online)</a>. For example, signing in to Google Drive through ChatGPT lets its plugin work with documents your account can already access. It doesn’t unlock other files or add Google Drive permissions.</p> <p>You may need to <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001494\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">connect your account (online)</a> or <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001495\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">approve an action (online)</a>. Available features depend on your app access, workspace settings, and where you use ChatGPT.</p> <p>Plugins with only skills and reference files need no app connection. For each required app, users need access and any account connection or action permissions the workflow needs. If an optional app is unavailable, other capabilities may still work; capabilities that require an unavailable app cannot.</p> <p><a id=\"example-plugin-page\"></a> <strong>Example Plugin Page</strong></p> <p>Here’s an example of a plugin page, showing its app and skills. The <strong>Disabled by admin</strong> label means this example plugin is not available to use in the workspace.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: An example Intuit QuickBooks plugin page, annotated to show its availability, sample requests, description, connected app, and included skills.</p> </blockquote> <p>With a custom GPT, you explicitly <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8554407-gpts-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">choose the GPT (online)</a> (by opening it or mentioning it with @ on ChatGPT web), then send it your request.</p> <p>With plugins, you can choose an available plugin or skill directly. In ChatGPT, <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001256-plugins-in-chatgpt-and-codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">use an @ mention or open + and select More (online)</a>, where supported.</p> <p><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/docs/codex/migrate-custom-gpts/invoke-plugin-hq.webm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Select a plugin from the ChatGPT composer (online)</a></p> <figcaption> Select an available plugin from the composer, then describe the task you want it to help with. </figcaption> <p>You can also describe your task: ChatGPT can <a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23?anchor=how-chatgpt-and-codex-use-skills\">automatically use a relevant installed skill</a>, including a skill packaged in a plugin, when its description matches what you need.</p> <p><strong>Test how your plugin gets selected</strong></p> <p>Automatic skill selection depends on the task and available capabilities; an installed plugin won’t run on every request. After migration, test both explicit selection and a normal task request.</p> <h3 id=\"what-can-a-plugin-do-compared-with-a-custom-gpt\">What can a plugin do compared with a custom GPT?</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>What you want to do</th> <th>With a custom GPT</th> <th>With a plugin</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Reuse instructions</td> <td>You add instructions to guide the GPT’s responses.</td> <td>A skill provides reusable instructions that guide how a task is done.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Use team knowledge</td> <td>You upload reference files as GPT knowledge.</td> <td>Skills can include reference files. Review the migrated resources and test how they’re used.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Connect to other services</td> <td>Custom actions connect the GPT to external services.</td> <td>Apps connect to services and supported actions. GPT custom actions need to be rebuilt separately.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Use tools and create files</td> <td>You enable available capabilities such as web search, image generation, and data analysis.</td> <td>Available tools depend on the experience and workspace settings. Test the outputs your team needs.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Start a workflow</td> <td>You open or explicitly select the GPT.</td> <td>You can select a plugin or skill. ChatGPT may also use a relevant installed skill automatically.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Share with your team</td> <td>You share the GPT with an allowed audience.</td> <td>You share or publish the plugin under workspace permissions. Review access before rollout.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h4>What transfers to a plugin</h4> <p><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/docs/codex/migrate-custom-gpts/01-what-transfers-hq.mp4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">What transfers to a plugin (online)</a></p> <p><figcaption id=\"01-what-transfers-description\"> <strong> See what moves into a plugin and what needs rebuilding. </strong> See how a GPT’s instructions and reference files become a skill and connected apps remain part of the plugin. Custom actions do not transfer; plan to replace them with a supported app’s read or write actions, or a custom MCP server. </figcaption> </p> <p><a id=\"plan-your-transition\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"for-admins-prepare-your-workspace\">For admins: Prepare your workspace</h2> <p>Help your team carry its work forward: agree on migration owners, check their permissions, and plan access to the replacements.</p> <ul> <li><strong>Admin notice.</strong> Admins receive an early heads-up and guidance to plan the transition and prepare their teams.</li> <li><strong>Migration.</strong> GPT creators and workspace admins can migrate published GPTs to plugins.</li> <li><strong>Custom GPT retirement.</strong> Custom GPTs stop working. Move the workflows you want to keep to plugins and test them before retirement.</li> </ul> <h3 id=\"choose-priority-migrations\">Choose priority migrations</h3> <p>Start with GPTs your team relies on most. Agree with their creators on what to keep, who will maintain it, and who needs access.</p> <ul> <li>Allow extra time for custom actions, which need to be rebuilt separately.</li> <li>Name an owner for each GPT and record its purpose, audience, instructions, reference files, and integrations.</li> <li>Ask owners to save a few familiar prompts and good results, including one harder case, so they can compare the replacement.</li> <li>Confirm which GPTs are published. Have creators publish needed drafts while GPT creation is still available; public sharing isn’t required.</li> </ul> <h4>Choose priority workflows</h4> <p><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/docs/codex/migrate-custom-gpts/02-prioritize-workflows-hq.mp4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Choose priority workflows (online)</a></p> <p><figcaption id=\"02-prioritize-workflows-description\"> <strong> Use ownership and recent usage to prioritize your GPT migrations. </strong> Identify the GPTs your team still relies on and consider leaving unused workflows behind. Admins with access to the ChatGPT admin plugin can request GPT names, owners, and message counts from the last 30 days to help prioritize. </figcaption> </p> <h3 id=\"review-workspace-permissions\">Review workspace permissions</h3> <p>Before migrating, check that everyone has the access they need. Permissions control actions such as using, sharing, or publishing plugins; roles group permissions for similar responsibilities. With <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11750701\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">role-based access control (RBAC) (online)</a>, workspace owners assign roles to people or groups.</p> <p>Use this table to check access for migration and the replacement plugins.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Action</th> <th>What admins should check</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Migrate their own custom GPTs to plugins</td> <td>Enable plugins for the workspace. The person migrating must be the GPT’s creator or a workspace owner or admin, and the GPT must be published. Having access to someone else’s GPT is not enough.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Share newly migrated GPTs (now plugins) with people or groups</td> <td>Give Share plugins to people who need to share replacements with individuals or groups. People who only use a plugin don’t need this permission.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Publish newly migrated GPTs (now plugins) to the workspace directory</td> <td>Give Publish plugins to workspace to people who will publish replacements in the workspace plugin directory. This is separate from sharing directly.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Install and use new plugins</td> <td>Allow Use plugins for the intended users or roles.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Use an included app</td> <td>Enable required apps for the intended users or roles. Check that their connected accounts can access the needed information. Only supported, allowed actions can run, and required approvals still apply. Plugin installation does not add app or file permissions.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><strong>Built-in migration doesn't require upload permissions</strong></p> <p>You do not need to enable <strong>Upload plugins</strong> or <strong>Upload plugins with custom MCP servers</strong> just for the built-in migration. Set any permissions for separately rebuilt integrations according to your workspace's policies.</p> <p>For current settings, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11509118\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Plugin and app admin controls (online)</a> and <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001066\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Skill admin controls (online)</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"check-installation-and-app-access\">Check installation and app access</h3> <p>Decide how teammates will get each replacement. Available lets eligible users install a plugin; Installed installs it for eligible users or roles. These settings do not change who the plugin is shared with.</p> <p>Review required apps separately: check workspace and role access, account sign-in, and action approvals. Test access with an account that has the same permissions as a typical teammate.</p> <p><a id=\"admin-bulk-migration\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"for-workspace-admins-migrate-gpts-in-bulk\">For workspace admins: Migrate GPTs in bulk</h4> <p>In ChatGPT Work, type <strong>@</strong> and select <a href=\"#/article/a-f094a985d5b867ef\">ChatGPT Admin</a>. Check that its Admin app shows <strong>Connected</strong>. For Codex, use the open or copy button on a prompt below. Review the prompt and selected plugin before sending.</p> <p><a id=\"1-inventory-and-prioritize\"></a> <a id=\"1-choose-the-gpts\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"1-run-the-gpt-report\">1. Run the GPT report</h3> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) Run the GPT report prioritizing by most recently used GPTs in the last 30 days.\n</code></pre> <p>The report is ordered by recent use and includes owners, usage, migration status, and custom actions.</p> <h4 id=\"optional-add-report-details\">Optional: Add report details</h4> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) Run the GPT report and include a summary of GPTs that haven’t been migrated.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) Run the GPT report and include which GPTs have knowledge files attached.\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"2-create-one-migration-tracker\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"2-export-and-use-the-results\">2. Export and use the results</h3> <p>Ask for your preferred format, such as <strong>Excel</strong>, <strong>CSV</strong>, or <strong>Google Sheets</strong>. Sort, filter, share, or track migration your way.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) Run the GPT report and export it as [preferred format].\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"6-help-teams-switch-and-repeat\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"3-schedule-a-recurring-report\">3. Schedule a recurring report</h3> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) Run the GPT report for [workspace] every [day] at [time and time zone]. Post the results here.\n</code></pre> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">Scheduled tasks</a> must be enabled, with the Admin plugin available to the task. Review the schedule and first runs in <strong>Scheduled</strong>.</p> <p><a id=\"3-migrate-a-small-batch\"></a> <a id=\"2-migrate-a-small-batch\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"4-migrate-selected-gpts\">4. Migrate selected GPTs</h3> <p>Choose GPTs by ID or describe the group, such as all private GPTs. Replacements start private, and originals become read-only.</p> <p><strong>Sharing settings do not carry over in bulk</strong></p> <p>Bulk migration <strong>does not copy sharing settings</strong>. Record who needs access, then <strong>share each replacement manually</strong> or ask the GPT creator to share it. We expect bulk sharing through the Admin plugin soon.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">[@ChatGPT Admin](plugin://admin-console@openai-curated-remote) Migrate [GPT IDs or a description of the GPTs] to plugins. Show me the selection and ask for confirmation before migrating.\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"4-test-and-refine\"></a> <a id=\"3-have-owners-test\"></a> <a id=\"5-share-and-check-access\"></a> <a id=\"4-share-and-confirm-access\"></a></p> <p>Have owners <a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=step-2-test-with-familiar-work\">test the replacement plugins</a> and verify access. Custom actions need to be rebuilt separately.</p> <p><a id=\"migration-email-template\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"email-template-ask-gpt-creators-to-migrate\">Email template: Ask GPT creators to migrate</h4> <p>Make this your own: replace the placeholders before sending.</p> <p><strong>Email template:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Subject: Please migrate your custom GPTs by [deadline]\n\nHi [name],\n\nWe’re moving our custom GPT workflows to plugins. Please migrate, test, and share these GPTs by [deadline]:\n\n[GPT names/links]\n\nIf you no longer need one, let us know. For those you’re keeping:\n\n1. Migrate. Save the intended audience and finish important edits first. Go to My GPTs &gt; Created by me &gt; Migrate to plugin. The GPT must be published; after migration, it becomes read-only.\n\n2. Test. Try familiar tasks and one harder case. Check the instructions, attached files, results, and required apps or tools.\n\n3. Share. Each replacement starts private. Share it with the intended people or groups, then ask a teammate to test access. Keep private workflows private.\n\nFollow [migration guide link] for the steps. Custom actions need rebuilding; contact [admin contact] if yours uses them or you need help.\n\nPlease reply with each plugin’s link, testing status, and any blockers.\n\nThanks for helping your team make the switch,\n[admin name/team]\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"identify-gpts-that-may-need-extra-attention\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"for-gpt-creators-prepare-your-gpt\">For GPT creators: Prepare your GPT</h2> <p>Before migrating a GPT you created, save its intended audience and a few familiar prompts and results for testing. Check the table below for anything that needs extra attention. Admins migrating on a creator’s behalf should review these details with them.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>If your custom GPT…</th> <th>What to review</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Uses custom actions</td> <td>Custom actions don’t transfer. Rebuild needed integrations with a supported connector or <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?sectionMissing=replacing-a-gpt-custom-action\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">custom MCP connection (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">Local page (section not recognized)</a>, then test them before your team switches.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Depends on a model, detailed instructions, or a strict format</td> <td>The selected model doesn’t carry over; Enterprise defaults apply. Compare familiar prompts and results. Check that the right skill is selected and follows your instructions and format, since behavior can differ.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Relies on files, tools, or previous chat context</td> <td>Check that files, templates, and examples are present and used correctly; transfer and retrieval may differ. Test required tools, such as web search, images, data analysis, or file creation. GPT capability settings don’t guarantee the same setup. Conversation starters and previous chats may not copy, so save useful prompts and identify needed context.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Is shared with teammates or people outside your workspace</td> <td>Record the intended audience and verify they can install and use the replacement. Show users how to install or select it. Check the replacement’s sharing settings. Check access for external users: public GPTs in affected Enterprise workspaces are included, but public sharing and timelines for other plans may differ.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Needs updates during the transition</td> <td>The original GPT stays usable until retirement. Maintain and test the replacement plugin as your workflow changes.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"migrate-test-and-share\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"for-gpt-creators-migrate-test-and-share\">For GPT creators: Migrate, test, and share</h2> <p>Use these steps for a published GPT you created. Workspace admins can also use them to help creators migrate individual GPTs.</p> <p><strong>Before you migrate:</strong> The original GPT becomes read-only after migration. You can continue using it until retirement, but future edits must be made in the replacement plugin.</p> <h3 id=\"step-1-convert-your-gpt\">Step 1: Convert your GPT</h3> <p>Go to <strong>My GPTs</strong>, find your GPT under <strong>Created by me</strong>, and select <strong>Migrate to plugin</strong>. You can also ask a workspace admin for help.</p> <p>Migration turns your GPT’s instructions into a skill and brings over its knowledge files and connected apps. Rebuild custom actions separately. Save familiar prompts: conversation starters do not transfer one-to-one. The selected model does not carry over, and capability settings do not guarantee the same tools or behavior. Review migrated files and test required tools before sharing.</p> <p>If you don’t see <strong>Migrate to plugin</strong>, see <a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=why-dont-i-see-the-migration-option\">Why don’t I see the migration option? (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97\">Local page (section not recognized)</a> in the Admin FAQ.</p> <p>Your new plugin starts private. Test it, then share it with the people who need access—even if they could already use the original GPT.</p> <p><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/docs/codex/migrate-custom-gpts/03-migration-walkthrough-hq.mp4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Watch the migration workflow (online)</a></p> <p><figcaption id=\"03-migration-walkthrough-description\"> <strong> Follow the migration steps, then review and install your plugin. </strong> This video shows an earlier app interface. In the current app, select <strong>Customize</strong>, then <strong>Plugins</strong>, in the left navigation to find your plugins. </figcaption> </p> <h3 id=\"step-2-test-with-familiar-work\">Step 2: Test with familiar work</h3> <p>Try the plugin on familiar tasks and one harder case. Check the following before sharing it.</p> <ul> <li>Is the right skill selected, and does it follow your instructions?</li> <li>Does it use the expected reference material and produce complete answers or files with the required structure, fields, and format?</li> <li>Does it handle the harder case correctly and respond in a workable amount of time?</li> <li>Are the tools and integrations it needs available?</li> </ul> <p><strong>Switch after the workflow is ready</strong></p> <p>If a required capability is missing, wait to switch that workflow until you have a tested alternative.</p> <p><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/docs/codex/migrate-custom-gpts/04-test-and-share-hq.mp4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Test before sharing (online)</a></p> <p><figcaption id=\"04-test-and-share-description\"> <strong> Test familiar workflows and refine the plugin before sharing it. </strong> </figcaption> </p> <h3 id=\"step-3-share-and-verify-access\">Step 3: Share and verify access</h3> <p>Review who can access the new plugin. To share with people or groups, you need Share plugins access. To publish to the workspace, you need Publish plugins to workspace. Have an intended user open and test the replacement.</p> <p><strong>For people using the replacement:</strong> After the creator or admin shares the plugin with you, install it before using it, unless your admin has installed it for you. Sharing access and installation are separate steps.</p> <p>If you can’t share or publish the plugin, ask your admin to check your permissions before announcing the switch.</p> <h3 id=\"step-4-help-your-team-switch\">Step 4: Help your team switch</h3> <p>Share the replacement link, explain key differences, and demonstrate a familiar task. Update onboarding, instructions, and saved resources, and name an owner for future changes and questions.</p> <p>After migration, the plugin’s creator or a workspace owner or admin can <a href=\"#/article/a-0d81218eacd2463c\">edit the replacement</a>. Rerun your important tests after each change.</p> <h3 id=\"what-happens-to-the-original-gpt\">What happens to the original GPT?</h3> <p>Until retirement, the original GPT stays usable, and you can continue editing an existing GPT that you have not migrated, even after new GPT creation stops. Once you migrate a GPT, the original becomes read-only. At retirement, custom GPTs stop running and leave the GPT directory.</p> <p><a id=\"troubleshoot-common-blockers\"></a> <a id=\"details-still-being-confirmed\"></a> <a id=\"additional-migration-questions\"></a> <a id=\"can-i-migrate-gpts-on-behalf-of-my-customers-or-users-including-in-bulk\"></a> <a id=\"can-we-migrate-or-recover-a-gpt-after-the-retirement-date\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"admin-faq\">Admin FAQ</h2> <p>Find answers to common questions about preparing your workspace and helping your team switch.</p> <p>h3]:mb-5 [&amp;&gt;h3]:mt-12 [&amp;&gt;h3]:text-xl [&amp;&gt;h3:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;<em>summary]:gap-3 [&amp;_summary]:px-5 [&amp;_summary]:py-4 [&amp;</em>.toggle-section-content]:px-5 [&amp;_details[open]&gt;.toggle-section-content]:border-t [&amp;_details[open]&gt;.toggle-section-content]:border-default [&amp;_details[open]&gt;.toggle-section-content]:pt-4 [&amp;_details[open]&gt;summary&gt;span&gt;svg]:rotate-90\"&gt;</p> <h3 id=\"preparing-your-workspace\">Preparing your workspace</h3> <p><a id=\"can-admins-migrate-many-gpts-at-once\"></a> <strong>Can admins migrate many GPTs at once?</strong></p> <p>Yes. Workspace admins can use the <a href=\"#/article/a-f094a985d5b867ef\">ChatGPT Admin plugin</a> to migrate selected batches. Start with the GPTs your team needs most.</p> <p>Use the <a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=admin-bulk-migration\">admin walkthrough</a> to run a report and migrate selected GPTs. Sharing settings do not carry over in bulk; share each replacement manually.</p> <p><a id=\"who-can-migrate-a-gpt-and-how-does-the-process-work\"></a> <strong>Who can migrate a GPT, and how does the process work?</strong></p> <p>The GPT’s creator or a workspace admin can start migration from a published GPT’s page. Admins can do this even if they did not create the GPT.</p> <p>Plugins must be enabled, and shared access alone does not give someone permission to migrate.</p> <p><a id=\"why-dont-i-see-the-migration-option\"></a> <strong>Why don’t I see the migration option?</strong></p> <p>You must be the GPT’s creator or a workspace admin, the GPT must be published, and plugins must be enabled for you.</p> <p>Access to use someone else’s GPT does not give you permission to migrate it.</p> <p>If these conditions are met and the option is still missing, contact OpenAI support with the GPT’s name, owner, and a description of what you’re seeing.</p> <p><a id=\"which-permissions-should-i-review-before-people-start-migrating\"></a> <strong>Which permissions should I review before people start migrating?</strong></p> <p>Start by enabling plugins. The built-in migration workflow does not require Upload plugins or Upload plugins with custom MCP servers.</p> <p>People who will share plugins with others in the workspace need Share plugins, and those who will publish them across the workspace need Publish plugins to workspace.</p> <p>Rebuilding a custom integration is a separate task and may require additional permissions.</p> <p><a id=\"what-do-employees-need-to-use-a-migrated-plugin\"></a> <strong>What do employees need to use a migrated plugin?</strong></p> <p>Employees need:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Use plugins</strong> permission.</li> <li>Access to the replacement plugin.</li> <li>A workspace policy that allows them to install it or installs it for them.</li> </ul> <p>Any included apps still require the appropriate app access and authorization. Connecting an account through ChatGPT does not give someone additional permissions in that app.</p> <p><a id=\"can-employees-use-migrated-plugins-in-chat-or-do-they-need-work\"></a> <strong>Can employees use migrated plugins in Chat, or do they need Work?</strong></p> <p>Migrated plugins can be used in Chat when plugins are enabled for the user, as well as in Work. Available tools still depend on the plugin, workspace settings, and where it is used. For the creation and editing workflow and its prerequisites, see <a href=\"#/article/a-0d81218eacd2463c\">Build plugins</a>.</p> <p>Check access for each task separately: using the plugin, creating or editing it, and sharing or publishing it. Before assigning maintainers, ask your admin to confirm that they can access the creation and editing experience; the built-in migration requirements do not answer that question.</p> <p><a id=\"how-should-i-manage-access-when-we-roll-out-the-replacements\"></a> <strong>How should I manage access when we roll out the replacements?</strong></p> <p>Review each plugin’s audience and <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11509118\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">installation policy (online)</a>, then ask someone in the intended audience to test access.</p> <p>An Available plugin lets eligible users install it, while an Installed plugin is installed for them by default. Role controls and app permissions still apply.</p> <p>The replacement starts private. Access to the original GPT does not automatically give someone access to the plugin. Share it with the intended people or groups, then ask a recipient to install and test it, unless their admin has already installed it for them. Identify who will maintain the replacement and help teammates with access.</p> <h3 id=\"testing-and-ongoing-administration\">Testing and ongoing administration</h3> <p><a id=\"will-a-migrated-plugin-behave-exactly-like-the-original-gpt\"></a> <strong>Will a migrated plugin behave exactly like the original GPT?</strong></p> <p>A migrated plugin may respond differently from the original GPT. Compare the same prompts and reference files, including one difficult example, and check that answers use the right sources, include the expected facts, follow the requested format, and use the required tools. Test both explicit plugin selection and a normal task request, since automatic skill selection depends on the request and available capabilities. Ask owners to assess:</p> <ul> <li>The quality of the output.</li> <li>How well instructions are followed.</li> <li>How long the task takes.</li> </ul> <p>The GPT’s selected model does not carry over; Enterprise defaults apply.</p> <p><a id=\"what-should-i-do-about-gpts-that-use-custom-actions\"></a> <strong>What should I do about GPTs that use custom actions?</strong></p> <p>Custom actions do not transfer through the migration workflow. The person maintaining that workflow will need to rebuild the integration using a supported connector or a custom MCP server. See <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?sectionMissing=replacing-a-gpt-custom-action\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">Replacing a GPT custom action (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">Local page (section not recognized)</a> for the steps and a prompt you can adapt.</p> <p>Identify these GPTs early so the appropriate technical and security teams have time to review the replacement and its permissions.</p> <p><a id=\"what-happens-to-the-original-gpt-after-migration\"></a> <strong>What happens to the original GPT after migration?</strong></p> <p>The original GPT remains usable until retirement. At retirement, custom GPTs stop running and leave the GPT directory.</p> <p>Owners should maintain the plugin going forward. See <a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97?anchor=what-happens-to-the-original-gpt\">What happens to the original GPT?</a>.</p> <p><a id=\"can-we-still-migrate-a-gpt-after-retirement\"></a> <strong>Can we still migrate a GPT after retirement?</strong></p> <p>Yes. You will still be able to migrate a GPT after retirement, although the GPT itself will no longer run.</p> <p><a id=\"which-admin-controls-apply-after-migration\"></a> <strong>Which admin controls apply after migration?</strong></p> <p>Migrated plugins follow the workspace’s <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001256-plugins-in-chatgpt-and-codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">plugin permissions (online)</a>. Admins can control who uses and shares plugins, as well as who publishes them to the workspace. You can review role permissions and manage individual plugins.</p> <p>Included apps retain their own access and action controls, so making a plugin available does not grant access to the data or actions in its apps.</p> <p><a id=\"how-should-admins-plan-for-plugin-usage-and-costs\"></a> <strong>How should admins plan for plugin usage and costs?</strong></p> <p>Converting a custom GPT to a plugin does not consume credits. Under credit-based pricing, editing or updating a plugin does consume credits. Conversion is separate from using the replacement plugin, so review the usage and costs of the workflow before rolling it out.</p> <p>Usage depends on whether the plugin runs in Chat or Work, the models and features involved, and your workspace’s agreement. Under credit-based pricing, Instant Chat is generally unlimited, but a request can switch to a reasoning model or use a feature that consumes credits. Work consumes credits based on the model and tokens used. Enterprise agreements billed in USD have different terms, including charges for Instant usage. Review your workspace’s <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11481834\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">credit-based rate card (online)</a> or <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001415\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">USD rate card (online)</a> before rollout.</p> <p>Review users’ effective usage limits and workspace spending controls separately. In a credit-based workspace, a zero overage limit prevents spending beyond the shared credit allocation; it does not prevent use of remaining credits. Usage alerts notify admins but do not stop usage. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001001\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Manage usage limits and overages (online)</a> for the controls that apply to your workspace.</p>"};
